00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:12.000
Cohesity addresses the problem
of mass data fragmentation.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.520
So let me explain to you
what this actually mean.

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:17.810
So you probably have hundreds
or thousands of applications

00:23:17.810 --> 00:23:20.070
and you backup
those applications,

00:23:20.070 --> 00:23:24.530
the data of those applications
into your storage silos.

00:23:24.530 --> 00:23:29.150
And you probably have 5, 6, 7
different management vendors

00:23:29.150 --> 00:23:31.380
to do this job.

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:34.020
So all of this
becomes very complex.

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:37.220
So there's a lot of
organizational and IT

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:39.210
complexity in here.

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:42.020
And then you probably
take copies of this data.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:44.220
You probably take 10
copies of this data

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:49.050
or perhaps even more for use
cases like test dev and so on.

00:23:49.050 --> 00:23:53.510
And so this really increases
just the inefficiency

00:23:53.510 --> 00:23:57.250
of having all of this data
across your organization.

00:23:57.250 --> 00:24:01.520
And then lastly, this
data now is so fragmented

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.860
and dispersed across
your organization,

00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:06.920
you probably don't even
know what data you have

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:09.680
and where you have those,
and so this exposes you

00:24:09.680 --> 00:24:11.960
to compliance risks.

00:24:11.960 --> 00:24:14.470
So we are addressing
this kind of problem--

00:24:14.470 --> 00:24:18.040
this problem of mass data
fragmentation with a single web

00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:21.610
scale platform,
which spans to cloud

00:24:21.610 --> 00:24:24.200
but also on-premises
and end points.

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:26.290
And what we do
here, we consolidate

00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:29.900
all of this complexity into a
single platform for use cases,

00:24:29.900 --> 00:24:35.560
such as backup, archiving,
disaster recovery, and also

00:24:35.560 --> 00:24:37.870
test dev and a few
other use cases.

00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:42.280
And you can also download from
our marketplace applications

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:50.080
to address use cases like
anti-ransomware or compliance

00:24:50.080 --> 00:24:52.870
applications, which then
help you to actually get more

00:24:52.870 --> 00:24:55.630
value all of your backup data.

00:24:55.630 --> 00:24:59.380
So we radically simplify
backup and recovery

00:24:59.380 --> 00:25:02.080
through this single
consolidated platform,

00:25:02.080 --> 00:25:06.520
and we provide capabilities here
like policy-driven automation,

00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:12.680
which allows you to eliminate
scripting and manual processes.

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.190
We provide Google-like
search, which

00:25:15.190 --> 00:25:20.110
allows you to identify
and search and recover

00:25:20.110 --> 00:25:23.720
individual files or VMs.

