And lastly, we do all of this
by greatly reducing your data

00:25:27.410 --> 00:25:28.290
footprint.

00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:32.210
And we are using here features
like global variable lengthy

00:25:32.210 --> 00:25:35.390
deduplication and compression.

00:25:35.390 --> 00:25:39.260
So as I mentioned before,
we do this across the cloud

00:25:39.260 --> 00:25:40.990
on-premises and endpoints.

00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:43.370
But just two days ago, we
launched a new service here

00:25:43.370 --> 00:25:44.750
at Google Next.

00:25:44.750 --> 00:25:48.060
So it's called Cohesity
cloud backup service.

00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:49.740
So this is very exciting.

00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:52.220
That's a backup as a service.

00:25:52.220 --> 00:25:55.490
And specifically, it
provides enterprise grade

00:25:55.490 --> 00:25:57.530
backup and recovery
for applications

00:25:57.530 --> 00:25:59.170
running in the Google Cloud.

00:25:59.170 --> 00:26:02.570
But today, we really want to
focus on the hybrid use case.

00:26:02.570 --> 00:26:05.540
And also here we
make it very easy

00:26:05.540 --> 00:26:08.300
and seamless to integrate
into the Google Cloud.

